  "source_ref": "Two-hop join: Sundance EMC2-DP Design Specification QCF51 Issue 3.3.0 section 8 \"FMC Pin-Out\" (carrier FMC position -> Trenz B2B pins JB1-JB3; coordinate-extracted; byte-identical doc shared by all EMC2 variants) joined to Trenz TEM0007 schematic SCH-TEM0007-01 rev 01 (CHD11-A; B2B_Connector sheet 3 JM1-JM3 pin -> net, FPGA U2 symbol sheets net -> MPFS250T-FCVG484 ball; every joined ball cross-checked against the U2 symbol pad name, e.g. B1_GPIO4_N -> GPIO4NB1 -> C15). NOTE: schematic documents assembly variant CHD11-A; the EMC2-MPFS250 ships TEM0007-01-CHE11-A. The FPGA symbol is the MPFS250T-1FCVG484I and no variant-dependent FMC routing appears on the B2B sheet, so the mapping is taken as variant-independent (CHD/CHE differ in temp/speed assembly). The module inverts pair polarity on 32 of 64 routed signals, incl. GBTCLK0 (P position -> XCVR_0A_REFCLK_N ball L20, N -> L19) - intentional routing, actual copper recorded. EXCLUDED DP0: the carrier wires DP0_C2M positions C2/C3 to module XCVR_RX0 (G20/G19) and DP0_M2C positions C6/C7 to XCVR_TX0 (F21/F22) - host TX/RX swapped relative to VITA 57.1 (and pair-inverted), so a compliant card cannot use DP0; left absent so the closed-world join reads incompatible. EXCLUDED as not FPGA-routed on TEM0007: LA16, LA24, LA27, LA28 (B2B pins JB2.72-88 even side are no-connect, red-X NC markers); LA30/LA32/LA33 (JB2.90-99 = module JTAG block: 91=JTAG VREF 3.3V, 93=TMS, 95=TDI, 97=TDO, 99=TCK, 90=GND - caution: an FMC card driving these LA positions would drive module JTAG); LA11_P (JB1.39 tied to the module +1.8V rail; LA11_N recorded alone, unusable differentially); SCL (JB1.32 -> CPLD net SC_BOOTMODE) and SDA (JB1.34 unconnected). FMC JTAG -> carrier chain, GA0/GA1 not B2B-routed. PRSNT_M2C_L reaches FPGA I/O via B0_HSIO88_P. Carrier-side population not verifiable (no EMC2 carrier schematic cached); module routes are direct (no series muxes) per schematic.",
